# Prettier reads `.gitignore` as well as this file, so `node_modules/`, `dist/`,
# `coverage/` and `.tmp/` are already out. What belongs here is the rest: paths git
# tracks that Prettier still should not own.

# Vendored from `mattpocock/skills` and pinned by `skills-lock.json`. Formatting these
# puts a diff between every file and its upstream, which `npx skills update` then has
# to merge through on every pull.
.claude/skills/

# npm's file, not ours. Prettier reformats it and the next `npm install` writes it
# straight back, so `format:check` fails on a tree nobody edited.
package-lock.json

# The recorded `claude -p` streams. Prettier has no `.jsonl` parser today and skips
# them, but a fixture is a recording — one reformatted by a future release would no
# longer be the bytes the stream contract was read from.
test/fixtures/claude-stream/

# caveman's `SKILL.md`, vendored as the evidence roma's own ruleset was derived from.
# `*.md` below already covers it and this entry is what keeps that true: the day
# Markdown is widened into, a reformatted copy would fail its hash test as though
# upstream had moved.
test/fixtures/caveman/

# Prose is hand-wrapped here — `CONTEXT.md`, the ADRs, `docs/agents/`. Prettier is
# scoped to code for now; widening it to Markdown is a deliberate change with its own
# commit, not something that arrives as a side effect of formatting a `.ts` file.
*.md
